%I A399944 #37 Sep 26 2026 00:39:47
%S A399944 1527,6487,23390,32047,34207,42127,51847,56887,59911,62287,64807,
%T A399944 65311,102529,226081,5309344,8018901,119748396,139254850,187768485,
%U A399944 1420027536,2910369540,3991789984,4783272844,4875047415,4991698215,6729183747,9127300595,10936715855,93549492780
%N A399944 Numbers k such that sigma(k) = phi(k) + tau(k)^5.
%C A399944 All squarefree terms of sequence A399944 are terms of sequence A399540, and vice versa.
%C A399944 From _David A. Corneth_, Sep 16 2026: (Start)
%C A399944 If a(n) = k = m*p where m and p are coprime and p is prime then we have sigma(k) = sigma(m*p) = sigma(m) * sigma(p) = phi(m) * phi(p) + (tau(m)*tau(p))^5 = phi(k) + tau(k)^5 and so sigma(m)*(p + 1) = phi(m) * (p-1) + tau(m)*32. Solving for p gives p = (tau(k)^5*32 - phi(m) - sigma(m) / (sigma(m) - eulerphi(m)). (End)
%C A399944 From _David A. Corneth_, Sep 19 2026: (Start)
%C A399944 Also terms: 1353505679320032, 1433088983635452, 2779027455350496, 2797310530714644.
%C A399944 The search from a(29)-a(40) was done using prime signatures and their permutations (essentially found from A055932). Let f(k) = sigma(k)-phi(k)-tau(k)^5. If f(k) = 0 then k is in the sequence. If k = m*p^e for p prime coprime to m and q > p prime and f(k) > 0 and p larger than any prime factor of m then f(m*q^e) > 0. This can be used to trim the search by prime signatures and their permutations.
%C A399944 For example f(2*prime(100)) = f(2*541) = 62 > 0 so for any q > 541 we have f(2*q) > 0. (End)
%H A399944 David A. Corneth, <a href="/A399944/b399944.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..40</a>
%H A399944 S. I. Dimitrov, <a href="https://github.com/Stoyan16/Numbers-k-such-that-sigma-k-phi-k-tau-k-5/blob/main/A399944">Python program</a> (GitHub)
%e A399944 5309344 is a term since sigma(5309344) = 10584000 = 2621376 + 24^5 = phi(5309344) + tau(5309344)^5.
%o A399944 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); sigma(f) - eulerphi(f) == numdiv(f)^5; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 16 2026
%Y A399944 Cf. A000005, A000010, A000203, A055932, A399226, A399540.
%K A399944 nonn,new
%O A399944 1,1
%A A399944 _S. I. Dimitrov_, Sep 16 2026
